  "title": "Erdős Problem #489",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $A\\subseteq \\mathbb{N}$ be a set such that $\\lvert A\\cap [1,x]\\rvert=o(x^{1/2})$. Let $ B=\\{ n\\geq 1 : a\nmid n\\textrm{ for all }a\\in A\\}. $ If $B=\\{b_1<b_2<\\cdots\\}$ then is it true that $ \\lim \\frac{1}{x}\\sum_{b_i<x}(b_{i+1}-b_i)^2 $ exists (and is finite)?",
